    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0051" n="43" xml:id="pg43"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/2463: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-24T00:00:00-05:00">June 24,
                        1941—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received June 25—11:13 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>234. Reference is made to my telegram No. 225. Minister for Foreign Relations
                    today stated to me enabling decrees had all been issued. Manager of Bank of
                    Republic informed Commercial Attaché<anchor n="65" xml:id="d41-f1"/> bank is
                    prepared to purchase platinum for account of Metals Reserve Company charging
                    only necessary expenses of the operation. He desires information regarding
                    price, terms, form of contract with Metals Reserve Company, shipping
                    arrangements, etc.</p>
                <p>Please instruct.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d41-f1" n="65" xml:id="d41-f1-content">
                <p>Merwin L. Bohan.</p>
            </note>
